Let's write your first Java program:

```java
public class Hello {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Hello World");
    }
}
```

Explanation:
• 'public class Hello' - Creates a class named Hello (must match filename)
• 'public static void main' - The entry point where your program starts
• 'String[] args' - Command line arguments
• 'System.out.println' - Prints text to the console
• Curly braces {} group code together

Let's learn about variables - containers that hold data:

```java
public class Variables {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        // Different types of variables
        int age = 25;              // Integer number
        double price = 19.99;      // Decimal number
        String name = "Alex";      // Text
        boolean isStudent = true;  // True/False

        System.out.println("Name: " + name);
        System.out.println("Age: " + age);
        System.out.println("Price: $" + price);
        System.out.println("Student: " + isStudent);
    }
}
```

